# Folder authorization failure regression - 2026-07-02

Command:

```bash
npm test -- --run src/domains/workspace/components/OpenFolderButton.test.tsx src/domains/commands/categories/workspaceCommands.test.ts src/domains/commands/registry.test.ts
```

Result:

```text
Test Files  3 passed (3)
Tests       41 passed (41)
```

Coverage:

- Empty-state `OpenFolderButton` loads an authorized folder into the current window.
- When `grantWorkspaceDirectoryScope` rejects with `permission denied`, Prism emits a global error toast.
- Authorization failure does not call `loadFolderTree`.
- Authorization failure does not open a new Prism window.
- Authorization failure leaves `workspace.rootPath` null and `fileTree` empty, avoiding a half-loaded workspace state.
- Command palette/menu `openFolder` path remains covered by workspace command and registry tests; `runCommand` still provides the command-level failure toast fallback.

Additional verification:

```bash
npm run build
npm run tauri:build:app-smoke
PRISM_APP_PATH=/Applications/Prism.app node scripts/run-app-smoke.mjs
```

All build and app-smoke steps passed.
